+In short, **keep correctness, growth conformance, and practical speed visible without confusing their meanings.**
+
+## Account for validation evidence
+
+Every maintained check-in gate, required CI job, and qualification has an executable work definition in the [shared qualification plan](scripts/ci_qualification.py), with its workload, execution conditions, timing applicability, and applicable growth witnesses. Local validation, CI, and maintained profiling use that same definition without duplicating operation-owned contracts.
+
+Normal runs automatically record source and workload identity, functional outcome, applicable growth evidence, elapsed time, and any target comparison. Multi-stage qualifications also report phase costs, and complete validation runs report actual total elapsed time. Measurement is part of running the check, not an optional second task.
+
+An approved numerical timing target is compared when applicable. An explicit maintainer decision that no numerical target applies does not suppress timing or count as a passed target. Unknown applicability, a missing approved target, or missing or invalid required evidence remains unresolved and fails validation where required.
+
+Review the evidence before handing work back. Fix functional and growth-contract failures. Investigate timing misses and unavailable comparisons; record the evidence and any explicit maintainer approval to proceed with an identified timing shortfall in GitHub. Opening a follow-up does not grant approval, and timing approval does not waive a growth or correctness obligation.
+
+Changing a declared growth bound, a reviewed test budget, an approved timing target, its workload, or its applicable conditions requires explicit review and maintainer approval. Do not reset expectations to match a regression, weaken required proof, or change safety timeouts merely to improve a result.
+
+In short, **evidence and review are mandatory; conformance failures block validation, while elapsed-time targets remain diagnostic.**
 
